/* ---------- Type: one Chinese face everywhere, an academic serif for English ----------
   Chinese: "UI CJK" only covers CJK code points and sits first in every stack, so all Chinese
   renders in Songti. Macs use the installed Songti SC (local(), nothing downloaded); Windows and
   others fall back to self-hosted Noto Serif SC, split into unicode-range slices so a page only
   fetches the slices for the characters it shows (no Google Fonts: unreliable in mainland China).
   English: Charter on macOS; Charis SIL (the open-source Charter) self-hosted for everyone else.
